
Storing a ROM:
	- GET the PRG size in the nes HEADER.
	- ALLOCATE memory to the ROM using the size.
	- STORE the ROM in the allocated array using the
		specifications of the MAPPER.
	- ...


DISASSEMBLE:
	INFRASTRUCTURE:
	>>
	  	- STRUCT { arr_str, size }
		- FUNCTION to DISASSEMBLE and store the data in arr_str.
			Param:	*struct, *rom, rom_size.
			Return:	BOOL.
	<<
	IDEA:
	- POINT to the stored ROM.
	- GET ROM size.
	- CALL the DISASSEMBLE function to READ the ROM.
	- ALLOCATE memory to STORE the strings using the size.
	>>
	  Use the MAPPER to understand the start addr of each
	  bank of the ROM. The Addr printed in the disassemble,
	  (ex: $FFFF), depend on the MAPPER configuration. But,
	  the idea is to use the MAPPER and the processor->pc
	  to know what command the processor is executing,
	  because the ROM addr and processor->pc can be not the
	  same.
	<<
	>>
	  The DISASSEMBLE function will store the result in the
	  string array.
	<<
